    <DataNode elementId="AT5G60600-MONOMER" textLabel="4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl pyrophosphate synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8GZR7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;GcpE&lt;/i&gt; encoding a protein with 4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate synthase activity, was first identified through sequence similarity with its &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; homologue |CITS:[11943178]|. The enzyme&apos;s activity was confirmed through complementation of the lethal &lt;i&gt;gcpE E. coli&lt;/i&gt; mutant |CITS:[11943178]| and its subsequent purification |CITS:[15650872]|. This enzyme converts |FRAME:2C-METH-D-ERYTHRITOL-CYCLODIPHOSPHATE| into |FRAME:HYDROXY-METHYL-BUTENYL-DIP| in the |FRAME:NONMEVIPP-PWY|. Further study of the enzyme properties showed that it requires an intact [4Fe-4S] cluster for full activity |CITS:[15650872]|. Moreover, in contrast to its &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; homologue homologue, the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; enzyme cannot utilize NADPH/flavodoxin/flavodoxin reductase as a reducing shuttle system. 5-deazaflavin semiquinone radicals, however, could perform this function |CITS:[15650872]|. The specific activity obtained for the reconstituted enzyme was 0.16 &amp;mu;mol.min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt;.mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; after storage of the enzyme in liquid nitrogen. In the light, the electrons required for the reaction catalyzed by GcpE are directly provided by the electron flow from photosynthesis via ferredoxin. In the dark however, the enzyme requires an electron shuttle: ferredoxin-NADP&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; reductase |CITS:[16480720]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G60600-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G60600.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8GZR7" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAO15446" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12378" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G60600.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G60600" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="79.5" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="79.5" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16480720" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11943178" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15650872" />
    </DataNode>
